{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-4 experiments all use scvi_n200, with config_014 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, 0.7250) as the current best. We have measured three of the four (image_encoder × fusion) cells for transformer aggregation with scvi_n200: imagenet_vit_l+weighted (0.7250), imagenet_vit_l+concat (0.7207), and resnet50+weighted (0.7131). The missing cell is resnet50+concat. Question: config_004 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + concat) completes this 2×2 matrix, clarifying whether the small accuracy gap between imagenet_vit_l and resnet50 is consistent across fusion strategies, and whether concat vs weighted interacts with the image encoder. Why this is the best use: With only 2 experiments left (this one + one final), the priority is to confirm we have fully characterized the high-performing region rather than exploring low-probability directions (pca_n2000 or singleprofile are unlikely to beat 0.7250 given scgpt's poor performance and the strong multiprofile+transformer signal). This experiment is the logical exploitation step in the best-performing sub-space. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high (~6–7 GPU hours, comparable to config_032's 6.22 hrs for the same resnet50+transformer architecture), which is acceptable given it directly informs whether any untested variant could outperform the current best."
}

